            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <p><strong>A Natural Guide For Raising Children And Nurturing Others</strong></p>
                <p>You won’t find anybody as nurturing as a Caregiver archetype.  They have the heart, nurturing prowess and ‘stickability’ to provide a child, or person in need with as much love, care and attention as they need.  They will multiply their nurturing efforts ten-fold until that person is no longer in need (and will extend it beyond). </p>
                <p>With a caregiver archetype, you have a lifelong guarantee of love and care courtesy of them, if you are lucky enough to know one.</p>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">
                <p><strong>Pureness of Heart</strong></p>
                <p>The Caregiver Archetype’s intentions are always pure.</p>
                <p>Caregivers have an innate need for everybody to feel the unlimited love and care that they have in their heart for everybody - nothing else is as important - according to the Caregiver archetype.  </p>
                <p>They have no agenda at all other than to help.</p>
                <p>Even if occasionally a Caregiver may appear to be superficial (usually when they can’t say no, or lie in an attempt to save your feelings) they are far from that.  They always have your best interests at heart.   </p>
                <p><strong>Advocate Of Kindness</strong></p>
                <p>If you want to learn how to develop or express kindness, then watch a Caregiver in action. They are the epitome of kindness, and they will relish in that notion too.  </p>
                <p>I imagine that if you are reading this, as a Caregiver, you’ll nod your head in approval as you acknowledge that you are indeed effortlessly kind. </p>
                <p>It’s a quality that you admire greatly, as do most people around you (even if they don’t always show it).  </p>
                <p>Thank you, caregivers, for your kind and loving nature.  </p>
                <p><strong>Sincere</strong></p>
                <p>In some ways, this quality might seem to be somewhat of a contradiction because a Caregiver Archetype does have a problem in saying no to people.  And they don’t like speaking truths that might hurt somebody's feelings, even if it’s an important truth! </p>
                <p>However, the intentions of a Caregiver are incredibly sincere, cut them in half, and you’ll see nothing but love and kindness.  It’s how they can be so sincere.  </p>
                <p>So if you happen to be around a Caregiver who has told you a little white lie to save your feelings, cut them some slack, they just want you to be happy and well.  And that’s not such a bad thing after all is it?  </p>
                <p>Caregivers are sincere in their intention, and that intention is always to help you and to make the world a better place. </p>
                <p><strong>Feels Joy In Helping Others</strong></p>
                <p>While sometimes helping others can be draining and time-consuming for a Caregiver Archetype you can be sure that they gain something from helping and usually that something is joy.  </p>
                <p>It’s probably safe to assume that most people like helping people, but a Caregiver? Well, they thrive on it.  </p>
                <p><strong>Reliable</strong></p>
                <p>If a Caregiver Archetype has focused their attention toward you or has made a promise to anybody in any way, you can be sure that they will fulfill their promise.  </p>
                <p>A Caregiver cares about the feelings of others immensely, and to let them down in everyday life, to a Caregiver is to let them down emotionally which is a definite no go.  </p>
                <p>They want you to know that they’ve ‘got you’ and their actions will always speak louder than words.  </p>
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Can Be Taken For Granted</strong></p>
                <p>Unfortunately, a Caregiver can help people who don’t appreciate the help. Others can manipulate Their kind nature for their gain, and in some cases, a Caregiver will fall for this heartless act over and over again (unless they’ve already experienced and learned the lesson and understood how to implement boundaries to protect themselves).  </p>
                <p>If you are a caregiver and you’ve lent money to people who have not repaid you.  Been given the undesirable tasks at work and don’t know why, been shouted at undeservedly, or blamed for things then you’ll be able to relate to this experience.  </p>
                <p>Learning how to say no, how to assert yourself and implementing checks and boundaries to protect yourself are all necessary to correct this weakness. </p>
                <p><strong>Can Feel Unfulfilled Emotionally</strong></p>
                <p>There’s so much love, kindness and purity of heart in a Caregiver that it can be difficult for them to feel the expression of these qualities toward themselves, from others.  </p>
                <p>It’s as though the love of others is limited and cannot fill up the deep valleys of a Caregivers' heart.  Which can lead them to feel unfulfilled emotionally.  </p>
                <p>The Caregiver needs to learn to accept other people's love in the different ways that they express it, they need to let go of their often unrealistic expectations on love and learn how to fill themselves up.  This way the valleys in a Caregivers' heart will never run dry, allowing them to have more energy and resources to fulfill their need of helping people.  </p>
                <p><strong>Can’t Say No</strong></p>
                <p>Caregivers, cannot say no to a person in need, even if the needs of the person are superficial!  </p>
                <p>This can lead to them being taken for granted and disrespected or even being considered superficial (which is so far from their intention it might as well be on the moon!). It can also lead to exhaustion as their valuable time is spent on tasks or experiences that they have no interest in.  </p>
                <p>When a caregiver learns that saying no promotes respect, helps people to understand and communicate with them better and gives them the space that they need to fulfill their hearts and souls -  and to care for those who really need it, they will find more joy, peace and time in their lives!</p>
                <p><strong>Have Difficulty In Their Own Self Expression</strong></p>
                <p>Because a Caregiver is always thinking of others, they find it difficult to express themselves or their needs.  They wouldn't want to burden anybody or cause anybody to do anything they don’t want to do.  </p>
                <p>A Caregiver probably won’t tell you that they need help with something - but it doesn’t mean that they don’t hope somebody would notice they need help. </p>
                <p>What they don’t see though is how the people around them would delight in seeing the Caregiver let go and let them know what they want for a change. </p>
                <p><strong>Can Take Over Situations Un-necessarily</strong></p>
                <p>Times of trouble are always the greatest teachers and the best opportunities for personal growth.  Difficult times help people to evolve into a better person.  </p>
                <p>However, if a Caregiver is around and you hit a problem, the Caregiver can jump in, take over the problem and apply all of the care and attention you need to solve it before you can blink! And definitely, before you’ve had a chance to understand why you had the problem in the first place.  </p>
                <p>A Caregiver sometimes needs to take a step back and let nature take its course.  It’s a tough lesson for a Caregiver to learn though because they cannot stand to see another person struggling.  </p>
                <p><strong>At Risk Of Burning Out or Martyrdom</strong></p>
                <p>Because a Caregiver can be so extreme in how they distribute their care and often forget to take care of themselves, they can burn out.  Just take a look at the faces of carers who help the elderly, or nurses, mums, or of people who work with children in the care system and you’ll see how tired they really are.  </p>
                <p>The job of caring is draining and as much as a Caregiver loves to help they are at risk of burning out if they don’t learn how to take care of themselves too.   Or they are at risk of reluctantly caring because they don’t know what else to do. </p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step4-back hover f-left">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step6 hover f-right">6. Greatest Challenge</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <p>The Caregivers greatest challenge is to learn how to love and care unconditionally without giving themselves away. And what we mean by this is without ignoring and sacrificing their own needs.</p>
                <p>This challenge is not going to be easy for a Caregiver to master, primarily since it will involve learning how to identify those who are really in need and those who need to help themselves.  It also involves being able to acknowledge that somebody needs help (or seems to need help) yet still walking away without getting involved or at least merely guiding them without getting involved. </p>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>It also involves the need for the Caregiver to understand why they are so compelled to help, and to look at what they are avoiding in their own life when they are focused on others. </p>
                <p>Some Caregivers may never master this challenge during this lifetime. Turning people away who a Caregiver perceives to be in need is a profound challenge for them.  As is the difficulty of discerning or taking a long hard look at themselves and for some Caregivers, it will be too much of a challenge to bear.</p>
                <p>Yet the lessons, teachings, and opportunities for the Caregiver to reconcile this challenge will be presented to them in abundance throughout their life, silently prompting them to master this challenge so that they really can go out into the world and make it a better place, without compromising themselves, or their own goals and dreams.</p>
                <p>Think about how a hospital has a triage system to assess the level of care or urgency of care that a patient needs - this is an essential tactic used in real life situations to treat those who need care.  This system or a version of it is essentially what a Caregiver needs to learn.</p>
                <p><strong>How A Caregiver Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>Awareness is always the first step to healing or reconciliation, if a Caregiver can understand and accept their hidden self and the reasons behind why they might do the things they do (even if the Caregiver perceives some of these traits as undesirable) then they start to accept themselves for who they are (something which is new to a Caregiver).  </p>
                <p>As a Caregiver starts to accept the parts of themselves that they have denied, sacrificed or have felt ashamed of, their perspective on the world will change.  An aware Caregiver is balanced in their approach to caring, more diligent and discerning too, which will help others in a much more profound way and they’ll be happy and fulfilled too.  </p>
                <p>And all it takes to achieve fulfillment is for the Caregiver to accept and acknowledge all of themselves (even the parts that they deem to be undesirable), and then work out strategies for helping others that serve both the Caregiver and the people or animals they help.  </p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step5-back hover f-left">5. Strengths/Weaknesses</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step7 hover f-right">7. Conclusion</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step7-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?> Archetype - Conclusion</h2>
                <p>Few archetypes are as giving and kind-hearted as Caregivers. Their altruism and caring nature allow Caregivers to make a big difference in the world, more often than not improving the lives of those around them.</p>
                <p>However, for most Caregivers, they make great sacrifices in their personal growth to meet their desire to help those in need.</p>
                <p>And because Caregivers cannot abide some of the qualities that they need to develop to attain a sense of balance in their life they can be easily tripped up in areas where their idealism and passion for caring become more of a liability than an asset. </p>
                <p>When a Caregiver Archetype can face their challenges, they will learn that everything is good, but in moderation.   They will also learn how to discern between those who need help, those who need guidance and those who can help themselves then they start to balance the personal conflicts that they might experience inside. When they accomplish this, they begin to create a harmonious and balanced life where they get to care AND achieve their goals in life. </p>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/joy.png">
                <p>What you have read so far is just an introduction and a tiny portion of what we can tell you about The Caregiver Archetype. It doesn’t matter where you are as a Caregiver in your journey; whether you’ve already heard your ‘call to action’ and may have started to implement the changes you must make to overcome your greatest challenge.  Whether you’ve already achieved a sense of ‘contribution.’  Or whether you have found this report to be eye-opening from the offset. </p>
                <p>The thing is, we ‘get you,’ we know your call to action or your greatest challenge, we know the lessons you have to learn and how you might respond to them, and if you felt as though we understood you, that was because we do.</p>
                <p>We know how to help you to uncover and reconcile the hidden aspects of your ‘self’ so that when you do, all internal conflict fades away and what is left behind is a balanced, whole and strong individual who can navigate life on their terms while connecting with the right people deeply.</p>
                <p>We have spent years understanding the Caregiver Archetype, and have built on and adapted Jung’s work to ensure that you achieve great success in your quest for liberation.</p>
                <p>We continue to learn more about you and update our content as you send in your life stories and experiences.</p>
                <p>Slowly and surely, we have understood how the Caregiver thinks, relates and connects.  Why they do what they do and what they need to discover to reach their full potential.</p>
                <p>This is how we know that many of the challenges you’ve faced and will face in the future have been and can be reconciled, even if you cannot see how at this moment in time.</p>
                <p>But to reconcile your ‘self,’ YOU need to understand more about yourself. You need to discover your little (and big) traits so that you can understand them, accept them and work with them, or change them (if they do not serve you).</p>
                <p>Life is fleeting, and you don’t have to live your life in conflict and disruption because of your disdain for freedom. You don’t have to stand by, and watch others make the changes to the world that you are so capable of doing.  You can make changes in the world, and you can learn to bring about change without feeling trapped by limitation. You just need to learn how.</p>
                <p>To learn how, you need to go much deeper into your psyche, and start to uncover the secrets that you keep even from yourself, you need to learn about the secret lives of your unexpressed world and understand how your underworld can cause conflict in your reality - and then you need to learn how to reconcile it.</p>
                <p>Once you’ve learned about your hidden self, you need to protect your newly found sense of wholeness.  You can do this by learning how hidden forces influenced by timing, affect different phases of your life, forces that are seeking to achieve wholeness and are prompting you to reconcile parts of yourself so that you can feel complete; this is all part of the process of individuation.</p>
                <p>Most people don’t realize that these forces exist and then when they walk into problems in later life they are completely mystified as to how the new challenges they face came about!</p>
                <p>If you can develop an awareness of these factors and build strategies into your life by reconciling them as part of the individuation process, you will be able to conquer your shadows before them conquering you.</p>
                <p>The Premium Archetype Analysis will help you develop an awareness of the depths of your soul, and it’s needs, and then it presents you with coping strategies and resources to help you satisfy your deepest desires so that you feel utterly fulfilled.</p>
                <p>Are you ready to learn what really drives you as a Caregiver? What secretly motivates and inspires you? And what you are afraid of? </p>
                <p>Are you ready to learn how you can unlock your true potential, while also staying true to who you are?</p>
                <p>But here’s the caveat, it’s not for everyone – you need to be willing to challenge yourself, to face your fears, you’ll need to admit to parts of yourself that you may not pride yourself in, and to ask and answer questions you haven’t asked yourself before.  But if you do this, then you start to accept all of yourself, or you’ll find the resources to make the changes that you feel that you need to make so that you can accept yourself and then with that acceptance, you start to grow, and steer your life to one that you have only ever imagined before.</p>
                <p>The Premium Archetype Analysis is not a quick-fix solution, nor an easy shortcut.  But it will present you with the keys to unlocking your ‘self’ and finding out who you are, and then it will help you create a road-map for creating who you want to be in the future - realistically without any hidden forces driving you in the wrong direction.
                <p>Are you ready to go deeper than you've ever gone before?</p>
